findings.problem:
Three placeholder families sit outside the phone model's 500 Hz to 8 kHz passband:
- the settle knock at 300 Hz, although SOUND-PLAN 4.4's table asks for it 'in a phone's band';
- the door stop knock at 340 Hz;
- the ticks at 9.5 kHz.

Check 14 does not flag them because none is a story cue. On the phone pass the director will hear no settle at the stop (29.0) and no ticks in the hush. Tick 04, at 42.968, is the only onset between 41.53 and 44.5.

The feel the director was asked to approve (SOUND-PLAN 'Your decisions' question 1) says 'the hush comes back as the doors open'. The 1.3 arc row for People says 'the hush as the doors open', and Intrusion says 'a short idle'.

Option (b), chosen because the measured idle shake is visible (BUILD_LOG Sound 1), cannot deliver this. In the blockout the idle runs 7.2 s (29.0 to 36.2), under:
- both unlatches (30.44, 31.94);
- both people getting out;
- both latches (34.5, 35.6).

The hush starts at 36.6, 1.0 s after the second door shuts. Option (d) was meant to avoid exactly that idle masking (section 6); G456-03 shows the cost. Round 04's gate questions do not tell the director the feel changed.
